 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are in the data as
+`apiKeys` (`docs/DATA.md`); each has one role:
+
+- `viewer` may only read: every `GET` route except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook` may also `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager` may do everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+A request without a key or with an unknown key gets 401 `unauthorized`,
+whatever the route. A known key without permission gets 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request with a known key and a method other than `GET` writes an audit
+entry, whether it succeeded or not (a refused or failed attempt is recorded
+with its status). `GET /audit` (managers only) lists the entries newest
+first:
+
+    { "id": 7, "at": "2026-10-28T10:00:00.000Z", "keyName": "Seed cook",
+      "method": "POST", "path": "/recipes/1/cook", "status": 200 }
+
+`path` is without the query string. Requests answered 401 have no key name
+and are not recorded.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
